from pathlib import Path
import html,re
P=Path
E=html.escape
labs=[]
def lab(title,body,cmds,qa):labs.append((title,body,cmds,qa))
lab('GitOps: Git declares, Argo CD reconciles','Git contains the desired state. Argo CD fetches this repository, renders each Helm chart, compares it with Kubernetes, and applies changes when sync is requested or automated. Kubernetes controllers then create pods. GitOps is pull-based delivery: CI can test and push Git changes without holding your cluster-admin credentials. Sync status and health are different: Synced means desired resources match live resources; Healthy means resource health checks pass. A deployment can be Synced and still Degraded.', [('Check prerequisites','kubectl config use-context docker-desktop\nkubectl get nodes\nkubectl get deployments -n ingress-lab\nkubectl get ingressclass traefik\ngit remote -v')], [('What is reconciliation?','A repeated compare-and-act loop that converges actual state toward desired state. Git polling detects new desired state; Kubernetes watches detect live changes.'),('Is Argo CD a CI build system?','No. Build, test, scan and push images in CI. Commit the desired image tag or digest; Argo CD delivers that declared state.')])
lab('Install the Argo CD control plane','Complete Lab 1 first. Use this repository root in PowerShell. The pinned community-maintained argo-helm chart 10.11.6 installs Argo CD v3.5.6. The setup also configures Traefik to publish 127.0.0.1 as the Ingress status address, so the default Argo Ingress health check can finish. This reports a local entry address; it does not test HTTP connectivity. This small local installation runs a single controller, server, repo-server and Redis, not a production HA installation. Allow extra cluster resources and image-download time. The setup script creates a restricted AppProject and three Applications in manual-sync mode; it does not sync them automatically. For a fork, change repoURL in all three Application files AND sourceRepos in the project file to your repository before setup.', [('Install all prerequisites for Lab 2','powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/argocd-setup.ps1'),('Inspect components','kubectl get pods,svc -n argocd\nkubectl get crd applications.argoproj.io appprojects.argoproj.io\nkubectl get applications -n argocd\nkubectl get appproject ingress-lab -n argocd')], [('What do the components do?','The API server serves UI/API and authentication. Repo-server fetches Git and renders manifests. Application-controller compares and reconciles resources. Redis caches data. ApplicationSet can generate Applications; it is optional in this lab.'),('Application versus AppProject?','An Application defines one source, destination and sync policy. AppProject limits allowed repositories, destinations and resource kinds. It complements Kubernetes RBAC; it does not replace it.')])
lab('Open the URL and sign in','Argo CD is exposed through the existing Traefik controller at http://argocd.lab.test:8080. The local values disable Argo server TLS so Traefik forwards ordinary HTTP; this is only a localhost exercise. The port-forward binds to 127.0.0.1. Add the hosts entry using an elevated editor. Keep the password out of Git and screenshots. After first login, change it using User Info → Update Password. Do not reuse this local HTTP configuration for a public server.', [('Terminal A: keep ingress access running','kubectl port-forward -n ingress-system svc/lab-ingress-traefik 8080:80 --address 127.0.0.1'),('Add this line to the Windows hosts file','127.0.0.1 argocd.lab.test'),('Read the initial password locally','$encoded = kubectl get secret argocd-initial-admin-secret -n argocd -o jsonpath=\'{.data.password}\'\n[Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetString([Convert]::FromBase64String($encoded))'),('Check Argo server health through ingress','curl.exe -i -H "Host: argocd.lab.test" http://127.0.0.1:8080/healthz')], [('Which credentials do I use?','Username admin and the initial password stored in argocd-initial-admin-secret. If you changed the password earlier, use the changed password; the initial secret is not a current-password lookup.'),('Why configure server.insecure?','Here it selects HTTP behind the local ingress, not anonymous access. Authentication remains enabled. Production should use trusted TLS and appropriate SSO/RBAC.')])
lab('Read the Application and adopt today’s workloads','Open Applications in the UI: lab-nginx, lab-prometheus and lab-grafana. Inspect Details → source repository, main revision, charts/<app> path, destination ingress-lab, and project ingress-lab. Each source uses the same original Helm chart with values.yaml and a matching releaseName. These Applications adopt the existing named resources without uninstalling them. There is no resources-finalizer, so deleting an Application preserves workloads by default. Inspect DIFF before SYNC; normal adoption adds Argo tracking metadata. Never use force/replace for this handover. The old Helm release records remain as frozen history: Argo CD uses helm template, not helm install, and does not update Helm release history. Do not run helm upgrade, helm rollback or helm uninstall for these three apps after adoption. The original scripts now block if these Applications exist.', [('Review the NGINX declaration','Get-Content gitops/applications/nginx.yaml\nkubectl get application lab-nginx -n argocd -o yaml'),('Sync all three, without installing the Argo CLI','powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/argocd-sync.ps1\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/argocd-check.ps1'),('Verify ownership and existing routes','kubectl get deployment nginx -n ingress-lab -o yaml\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/smoke-test.ps1')], [('Does Argo CD install a Helm release?','No. It renders Helm manifests and manages Kubernetes resources itself. helm list can still show the old frozen records from Lab 1; those records are not current GitOps state.'),('Why keep the existing resource names and namespace?','They let Argo CD adopt the intended resources without creating parallel apps. Inspect the diff to confirm identity and avoid an accidental replacement.')])
lab('Manual sync: change Git, inspect diff, deploy','Start with manual sync. Edit only charts/nginx/values.yaml, changing replicaCount from 2 to 3, then commit and push. Use your fork URL if you are a student. Refresh asks Argo to compare; it does not deploy. Expect OutOfSync while live replicas remain 2. Open DIFF to see desired 3 versus live 2, then SYNC. Wait for Healthy and three replicas. Finally restore replicaCount to 2 in Git, commit, push, refresh and sync again. The standard check script expects the baseline two replicas.', [('Change the desired replica count in Git','$path = "charts/nginx/values.yaml"\n(Get-Content $path -Raw).Replace("replicaCount: 2", "replicaCount: 3") | Set-Content -Encoding utf8 $path\nhelm lint ./charts/nginx --strict\ngit add charts/nginx/values.yaml\ngit commit -m "Practice GitOps: scale nginx to three replicas"\ngit push origin main'),('Request comparison and inspect current state','kubectl annotate application lab-nginx -n argocd argocd.argoproj.io/refresh=hard --overwrite\nkubectl get application lab-nginx -n argocd\nkubectl get deployment nginx -n ingress-lab'),('Apply the Git state','powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/argocd-sync.ps1 -App nginx\nkubectl get deployment nginx -n ingress-lab'),('Restore two replicas through Git','$path = "charts/nginx/values.yaml"\n(Get-Content $path -Raw).Replace("replicaCount: 3", "replicaCount: 2") | Set-Content -Encoding utf8 $path\ngit add charts/nginx/values.yaml\ngit commit -m "Restore nginx baseline to two replicas"\ngit push origin main\nkubectl annotate application lab-nginx -n argocd argocd.argoproj.io/refresh=hard --overwrite\n# Wait until Details shows the new Git revision, then:\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/argocd-sync.ps1 -App nginx')], [('Refresh versus sync?','Refresh recalculates comparison, and hard refresh also invalidates cached manifests. Sync applies desired manifests. A refresh can lead to deployment only when automated sync is enabled.'),('What proves the change came from Git?','The Application’s resolved commit SHA, the desired/live diff and sync operation history link the rollout to the pushed commit, rather than a local uncommitted edit.')])
lab('Automated sync and self-healing','For permanent policy changes edit the Application YAML in Git, commit/push, then kubectl apply the declaration. These bootstrap Applications are not themselves managed by a parent Application, so pushing a policy file alone does not update the live Application. Auto-sync deploys Git changes; selfHeal repairs live drift even when the Git commit has not changed. Start with prune false. After applying the policy, manually scale NGINX to 1. Observe Argo CD restore spec.replicas to the Git value 2, then wait for 2/2 ready. Do not use this technique where an HPA is meant to own replicas without first planning field ownership.', [('Create the practice auto-sync policy','powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/argocd-policy.ps1 -Mode Auto\ngit add gitops/applications/nginx.yaml\ngit commit -m "Enable nginx auto-sync and self-healing"\ngit push origin main\nkubectl apply -f gitops/applications/nginx.yaml'),('Create drift and watch repair','kubectl scale deployment nginx -n ingress-lab --replicas=1\nkubectl get deployment nginx -n ingress-lab -w\n# Ctrl+C after spec replicas returns to 2 and both pods are ready.\nkubectl get application lab-nginx -n argocd\nkubectl rollout status deployment/nginx -n ingress-lab --timeout=180s')], [('Auto-sync versus selfHeal?','Auto-sync delivers a changed desired state from Git. selfHeal also triggers correction for cluster-only changes at the same Git revision.'),('Why did my kubectl edit disappear?','With selfHeal enabled, Git remains authoritative for managed fields. Commit the intended change instead of repeatedly editing the cluster.')])
lab('Pruning: delete only what Git removed','Pruning deletes resources previously tracked by this Application when they disappear from desired manifests. It does not delete arbitrary unrelated ConfigMaps. Use only the disposable gitops-prune-demo ConfigMap for practice. Keep automatic prune false and use an explicit UI SYNC with PRUNE checked for the removal. This separates Git removal, OutOfSync detection, and deletion. Never practice pruning on Prometheus data or namespaces.', [('Add a disposable chart template','Copy-Item gitops/exercises/prune-demo.yaml charts/nginx/templates/prune-demo.yaml\ngit add charts/nginx/templates/prune-demo.yaml\ngit commit -m "Practice GitOps: add disposable prune demo"\ngit push origin main\nkubectl annotate application lab-nginx -n argocd argocd.argoproj.io/refresh=hard --overwrite\n# Wait for auto-sync or manually sync after the new revision is visible.\nkubectl get configmap gitops-prune-demo -n ingress-lab'),('Remove it from desired state','git rm charts/nginx/templates/prune-demo.yaml\ngit commit -m "Practice GitOps: remove disposable prune demo"\ngit push origin main\nkubectl annotate application lab-nginx -n argocd argocd.argoproj.io/refresh=hard --overwrite\n# In UI: lab-nginx → SYNC → enable PRUNE → SYNCHRONIZE.\nkubectl get configmap gitops-prune-demo -n ingress-lab\n# Expected after prune: NotFound.')], [('Why can a deleted Git resource remain live?','Without pruning, Argo CD leaves it live and reports that it requires pruning. Removing a manifest alone is not always permission to delete the live resource.'),('What protects against an empty application deleting everything?','Automatic pruning normally keeps allowEmpty false. It is a safety guard, not a substitute for review, backups and restricted permissions.')])
lab('Explore the UI and optional CLI','UI tasks: inspect the resource tree; select a Deployment and view desired/live manifests, events and pod logs; use DIFF before SYNC; check History and Rollback to identify revisions. Refresh is cheaper than Hard Refresh; use hard refresh for suspected stale rendering. Do not click DELETE with cascading deletion enabled. Optional CLI commands below require a matching official Argo CD CLI already installed. The full lab works using UI and kubectl without it. --grpc-web carries CLI requests over this HTTP ingress.', [('Optional CLI login and inspection','argocd login argocd.lab.test:8080 --username admin --plaintext --grpc-web\n# Enter password interactively; do not put it in command history.\nargocd app list --grpc-web\nargocd app get lab-nginx --grpc-web\nargocd app diff lab-nginx --grpc-web\nargocd app history lab-nginx --grpc-web\nargocd app sync lab-nginx --grpc-web\nargocd app wait lab-nginx --sync --health --timeout 180 --grpc-web'),('Get the same status with kubectl','kubectl get applications -n argocd\nkubectl get application lab-nginx -n argocd -o jsonpath=\'{.status.sync.revision}\'\nkubectl get application lab-nginx -n argocd -o jsonpath=\'{.status.operationState.message}\'')], [('When should Hard Refresh be used?','When comparison may be using stale repository/render caches; it forces fresh manifest generation. It is not a fix for invalid YAML, missing permissions or unhealthy pods.'),('What is a Helm parameter override?','An Application-level override can take precedence over values.yaml, so the chart file may not explain effective desired state. Prefer reviewed Git values and inspect Application parameters during troubleshooting.')])
lab('Rollback by Git revert and understand ownership','The preferred GitOps rollback is a new commit that reverts the bad change, followed by reconciliation. If auto-sync is enabled, an imperative rollback can be blocked or later replaced by the current Git head. Use a specific single-purpose commit SHA; inspect the diff before reverting. The Application definitions are bootstrapped with kubectl; their child workloads are Git-managed. App-of-apps or ApplicationSet is a later exercise for managing the Application lifecycle itself.', [('Inspect and revert a practice commit','git log --oneline -8\n# Replace BAD_COMMIT with the SHA of your own single-purpose practice change:\ngit revert BAD_COMMIT\ngit push origin main\nkubectl annotate application lab-nginx -n argocd argocd.argoproj.io/refresh=hard --overwrite\n# Manual-sync policy? Inspect diff and sync. Auto-sync? Watch reconciliation.')], [('Why revert rather than reset and force-push?','Revert preserves an auditable history and works cleanly with shared branches. Force-pushing rewrites history and complicates review and correlation.'),('Why does pushing an Application policy YAML not change policy automatically?','In this design no parent Application watches gitops/applications. Reapply the YAML after committing it, or deliberately introduce an app-of-apps lifecycle later.')])
lab('Troubleshoot with evidence','Use the Application conditions and operation message first. ComparisonError often means a repository fetch or rendering problem. SyncFailed can mean API validation or AppProject restrictions. Synced + Degraded usually needs pod readiness, image pulls, resource or application debugging. Do not fix persistent state by blindly clicking Force or Replace. For a private fork, connect it through Settings → Repositories with narrowly scoped credentials stored in Kubernetes Secrets, never committed to this repo. A public repo normally needs no repository credential.', [('Read errors and component logs','kubectl get application lab-nginx -n argocd -o yaml\nkubectl get events -n ingress-lab --sort-by=.lastTimestamp\nkubectl logs -n argocd statefulset/argocd-application-controller --tail=50\nkubectl logs -n argocd deployment/argocd-repo-server --tail=50\nkubectl describe pods -n ingress-lab'),('Recheck the rendered chart and routes','helm lint charts/nginx --strict\nhelm template nginx charts/nginx -n ingress-lab\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/argocd-check.ps1\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/smoke-test.ps1')], [('OutOfSync versus Degraded?','OutOfSync is a desired/live comparison result. Degraded is a health result. They answer different questions and can occur independently.'),('Why is a valid manifest denied?','The AppProject may disallow that repository, destination or resource kind, or Kubernetes RBAC/admission may deny the API request. Read the actual error before changing permissions.')])
lab('Pause management, restore baseline and clean up deliberately','End practice with replicaCount 2, no prune-demo template, and manual sync policy in the committed nginx Application. Apply the baseline Application and sync all three. The control plane can remain installed for learning. To return management to Helm, first remove the Argo Applications WITHOUT cascading deletion, verify they are gone, then use the Lab 1 Helm deployment script to reconcile the frozen Helm records to the current chart. Do not uninstall a frozen application Helm release while Argo still owns it. The commands below explicitly preserve workloads.', [('Final baseline checks','git status --short\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/argocd-policy.ps1 -Mode Manual\ngit add gitops/applications/nginx.yaml\ngit commit -m "Restore manual GitOps baseline"\ngit push origin main\nkubectl apply -f gitops/applications/\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/argocd-sync.ps1\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/argocd-check.ps1'),('Optional hand-back to Helm; preserves workloads','kubectl get applications -n argocd -o yaml\n# Confirm these lab Applications have NO resources-finalizer before deletion.\nkubectl delete application lab-nginx lab-prometheus lab-grafana -n argocd --cascade=orphan\nkubectl get deployments -n ingress-lab\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/deploy.ps1'),('Optional Argo CD control-plane removal after hand-back','kubectl delete ingress argocd -n argocd\nkubectl delete appproject ingress-lab -n argocd\nhelm uninstall argocd -n argocd\n# Namespace and CRDs may remain; do not blindly delete shared CRDs or namespaces.')], [('What is cascading Application deletion?','With the Argo resources-finalizer, deleting an Application can delete its managed resources. These examples intentionally omit that finalizer. Check live metadata before deleting.'),('Can Helm and Argo manage the same workloads simultaneously?','They can issue conflicting updates. Choose one active owner; freeze Helm during GitOps and deliberately hand back ownership before running its lifecycle commands.')])

# Bash-first commands; legacy PowerShell helpers remain optional compatibility files.
